{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Good Leadership", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Becoming a Good Leader", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the root of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the main part of something, from which other things have developed ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is said that effective communication skills are at the root of excellent management.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about managers. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "key skill", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an ability to do something that is necessary ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Assertiveness is claimed to be an important key skill for managers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tactful", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not likely to upset or embarrass other people ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a manager, your communication style ought to be consistent, clear and tactful.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "execution", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a process in which you do something that has been carefully planned", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Managers need to oversee the execution of it all and provide constructive feedback.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "viewpoint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a particular way of thinking about a subject", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's possible to be assertive while also respecting the other person's viewpoint.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to follow through", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do what needs to be done to complete something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A manager should be explicit with expectations and plans and follow through with actions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "compensation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bcombination of \u200bmoney and other \u200bbenefits that an \u200bemployee \u200breceives for doing \u200btheir \u200bjob", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A good manager is known to individually consider each employee and try to match their talents and interests with their tasks and compensation.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to distribute", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to share things among a group of people, especially in a planned way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Putting the puzzle together efficiently involves distributing tasks and coming up with strategies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hesitate", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to pause before saying something because you are nervous or not sure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You ought to be able to communicate your ideas in a confident way without hesitating.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Report Verbs with Impersonal Passive Constructions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to avoid saying the generalized agent (<span class=\"italic\">they</span>, <span class=\"italic\">people</span>, <span class=\"italic\">everybody</span> etc.) of an action, you can use report verbs such as <span class=\"italic\">say</span>, <span class=\"italic\">believe</span>, <span class=\"italic\">think</span>, <span class=\"italic\">claim</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> mention</span>, <span class=\"italic\">request</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">point out </span>with a passive structure.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "This structure is called the <span class=\"strong\">impersonal passive</span>. <br>Take a look at the following examples. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Active voice: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">They say women are stronger than men. </span><br> In this case, you can avoid saying who thinks or says something by changing the subject (they)  to <span class=\"strong\">it</span> and the <span class=\"strong\">reporting verb</span> (say) to the passive. <br> The sentence would be: <br> <span class=\"strong\">It is said </span> that women are stronger than men.<br> What happens when the second verb (<span class=\"strong\">are</span> in this case) is presented in a different tense?<br> The answer is that the tense does not change in the <span class=\"strong\"> impersonal passive</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the examples in the chart below:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It<span class=\"strong\"> is said </span>that effective communication skills are at the root of excellent management. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A good manager<span class=\"strong\"> is known </span>to individually consider each employee and try to match their talents and interests with their tasks and compensation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It<span class=\"strong\"> is assumed</span> that employees, tasks and goals are the puzzle pieces.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It<span class=\"strong\"> is understood</span> that being a good manager and incorporating all six of the skills requires a lot of hard work and dedication.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Active voice </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Impersonal passive </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Everybody knows that my mother likes red wine. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It is known that  my mother likes red wine. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">People claim that money was the most important thing in that time. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">It is claimed that money was the most important thing in that time. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Experts believe that medicine has improved over the years.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It is believed that  medicine has improved over the years. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">They think that he will arrive soon. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It is thought that he will arrive soon.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">People presume  that the president of the company is having a meeting in London. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It is presumed  that the president of the company is having a meeting in London. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modals for Expressing Duty and Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">should</span> and <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> to provide suggestions. There are slight differences when using those modal verbs.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ought to</span> <br> We use <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span>: <br><br> to express that something is the desired or ideal thing to do, especially when there is some moral reason to do so. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">You ought</span> to admit that you plagiarized the article. </span><br><br> to predict that something is expected under normal conditions. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">The letter <span class=\"strong\">ought to </span>arrive tomorrow morning. </span><br><br>  to offer or ask recommendations. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">If you haven't studied the topic, you <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> start now. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Should</span> <br> We use <span class=\"strong\">should</span>: <br><br>  to express that something is the right thing to do because it is a duty. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\"> All students <span class=\"strong\">should </span> be provided with a proper desk. </span> <br><br>  to give or ask suggestions. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should </span> see a doctor. You don't look okay. </span>  <br><br>  to predict that something will happen under normal conditions. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">By next month. I<span class=\"strong\"> should have</span>  visited many places. </span><br><br>  The form of these structures is: <br> subject + should/ought to + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "As a manager, your communication style ought to be consistent, clear and tactful.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You should use the appropriate words to communicate your ideas, requests and concerns.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They ought to be able to interact with others in an informal but professional manner.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " A manager should be explicit with expectations and plans and follow through with actions.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "In pairs, brainstorm a person who you both know that is a manager.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It could be a boss, teacher, or coach.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Using the six skills that make a good manager, for each category (communication style, assertiveness) give a score between 1 and 4.  (1 being the lowest and 4 being the highest).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your ranking with another group and explain your reasoning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Then, using the six skills that make a good manager, assess whether or not you would be a good manager using the same process as before.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write an analysis of your strengths and your weaknesses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I collaborate with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I analyze an individual example and based on a scale assess their effectiveness as a manager.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I self-reflect and analyze my own strengths and weaknesses as a possible manager.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, 